<title>ITALY: Monte dei Paschi of Italy cuts prime rate.</title>
<headline>Monte dei Paschi of Italy cuts prime rate.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian bank Monte dei Paschi di Siena said on Thursday it had cut its prime rate to 10 percent from 10.75 and its top rate to 17.75 from 18.50 in response to the Bank of Italy's discount rate cut.</p>
<p>The cut was the first from a commercial bank since the central bank announced on Wednesday it was lowering the discount rate by 75 basis points to 7.50 percent, effective Thursday.</p>
<p>--Rome newsroom +39 6 6782505</p>
</text>
